---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { organization, specification, sdks, url } from '../../../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="ANS implementations"
  description="Explore the ANS reference implementation, Go, Rust, and Java SDKs, gateway integrations, OpenShell research preview, and related Trust Index work."
>
  <section class="container page-head">
    <div class="grid page-head-grid">
      <h1 class="c-1-7">Software you can build with</h1>
      <p class="lead c-8-12">
        Explore the code you can build with today, the examples you can learn
        from, and the previews you can help shape.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <hr class="page-rule container" />

  <section class="section section--s">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Core implementation and SDKs</h2>
      <div class="rows">
        <article class="grid integration-row">
          <div class="c-1-4">
            <h3>Registration Authority and Transparency Log</h3>
            <p class="tag">Reference implementation</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c-5-12">
            <p>
              A Go implementation of the registration lifecycle and transparency
              services, with local demos and an offline verifier. Run it to
              understand the protocol or evaluate your own deployment.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href={`${organization}/ans`}>Explore ans</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        {sdks.map((sdk) => (
          <article class="grid integration-row">
            <div class="c-1-4">
              <h3>{sdk.name}</h3>
              <p class="tag">{sdk.label}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="c-5-12">
              <p>
                {sdk.detail} Check the repository’s releases and documentation
                for the exact supported API and verification features.
              </p>
              <p>
                <a href={`${organization}/${sdk.repo}`}>Explore {sdk.repo}</a>
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--s">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Integrations and examples</h2>
      <div class="rows">
        <article class="grid integration-row">
          <div class="c-1-4">
            <h3>agentgateway and Agent Router</h3>
            <p class="tag">Verifier and gateway recipes</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c-5-12">
            <p>
              <code>ans-gateway-auth</code> verifies ANS-6 Method B callers
              through Envoy’s external authorization protocol. It includes
              gateway recipes and end-to-end suites for agentgateway and Agent
              Router.
            </p>
            <p>
              Support for other Envoy-compatible gateways depends on their
              configuration and request forwarding. The repository documents
              that coverage boundary.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href={`${organization}/ans-gateway-auth`}>
                Source and deployment recipes
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid integration-row">
          <div class="c-1-4">
            <h3>NVIDIA OpenShell</h3>
            <p class="tag">Research preview</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c-5-12">
            <p>
              <code>ans-openshell</code> adds signing middleware and destination
              registration checks outside an agent’s sandbox, keeping its
              identity key out of the sandbox.
            </p>
            <p>
              Its upstream extension contracts are previews. Destination
              registration checks do not implement ANS-6 binding to the actual
              TLS peer certificate; see the repository’s security notes.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href={`${organization}/ans-openshell`}>
                Explore the research preview
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid integration-row">
          <div class="c-1-4">
            <h3>A2A, MCP and HTTP</h3>
            <p class="tag">SDK examples</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c-5-12">
            <p>
              Use the SDK examples as starting points for adding ANS
              verification to protocol clients and services. Protocol
              compatibility still requires an application to wire in and enforce
              verification.
            </p>
            <ul class="link-list">
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`${organization}/ans-sdk-java/tree/main/ans-sdk-agent-client/examples`}
                >
                  Java protocol examples
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`${organization}/ans-sdk-rust/blob/main/crates/ans-verify/examples/mcp_mtls_client.rs`}
                >
                  Rust MCP client
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--s">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Related work</h2>
      <div class="rows">
        <article class="grid integration-row">
          <div class="c-1-4">
            <h3>DNS-AID alignment</h3>
            <p class="tag">Discovery profile</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c-5-12">
            <p>
              The published <code>ANS_DNSAID</code> profile uses SVCB records
              for endpoint discovery. ANS adds registration and authentication
              evidence. Read the profile for its current record format.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a
                href={`${specification}/blob/main/spec/discovery-profiles/ans-dnsaid.md`}
              >
                Read the profile
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid integration-row">
          <div class="c-1-4">
            <h3>Trust evaluation</h3>
            <p class="tag">Separate project</p>
          </div>
          <div class="c-5-12">
            <p>
              The Trust Index specification and Agent Trust Discovery reference
              implementation explore scoring with ANS evidence and other
              signals. Scoring is separate from ANS authentication; the
              implementation documents deferred features.
            </p>
            <ul class="link-list">
              <li>
                <a href={`${organization}/trust-index-spec`}>
                  Trust Index specification
                </a>
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href={`${organization}/agent-trust-discovery`}>
                  Reference implementation
                </a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--l">
    <div class="container grid ruled">
      <h2 class="c-1-5">Bring your framework</h2>
      <div class="c-7-12 prose-split">
        <p>
          A framework can call an ANS SDK, API, or gateway verifier, but an
          integration must enforce the verification result in the request path.
          Adding a tool to an agent’s tool list alone does not guarantee that it
          will be used.
        </p>
        <p>
          Have an adapter to share? Open an issue with the public source,
          installation instructions, supported ANS features, and tests that
          demonstrate rejected invalid requests.
        </p>
        <a class="link-action" href={url('community/')}>
          Contribute an integration
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
